/--
An ungated `invalid` verdict of `Boolean` at `Base` is one whose open branch did not pass all
eight hypotheses of `not_valid_of_hasOpen_int`, so the countermodel has no theorem behind it.
**The conjecture**: every such formula is not derivable at `Base`. Measured count at the ruled
bound (complexity 5, a two-atom pool): **0** (exhaustive over the fragment at that bound).
-/
def enumeratedBooleanBaseInvalid : Conjecture where
  statement := ∀ φ : Formula,
    (profileF φ).fragment = Fragment.Boolean → φ.complexity ≤ 5 →
    (decideAuto φ FrameClass.Base).isInvalid = true →
    ¬ Nonempty (DerivationTree FrameClass.Base [] φ)
  fragment := .Boolean
  ops := {}
  frameClass := some .Base
  status := .heuristicallyRefuted
  note := "0 formulas in this cell at complexity 5 over a 2-atom pool; exhaustive over the \
    fragment at that bound. A gated invalid verdict is a certified refutation rather \
    than a conjecture and is written to data/theorem-library-countermodels.jsonl; \
    only the ungated ones are counted here. The per-formula records are in \
    data/theorem-library-pipeline.jsonl."

